in 2009 I went out to Zambia and I  visited a rural village where there was  no drinking water and I met this little  boy he was 5 years old and he would walk  12 kilometer round trip to collect clean  water and I just I just couldn't believe  that he would walk that far  and after doing some investigation it  was true and I remember as a teenager  vowing to God that if everyone becomes  successful you have all become rich I'm  gonna go back to that village and build  a a water Wow or a borehole  and to be able to provide drinking water  but I only thought boy but the whole  village of 350 people and a few years  later I was financially free in property  and I remember that boy I remembered the  village and I went back and I built a  borehole 110 meters deep and I couldn't  remember the spring water coming up and  all the local children and the village  is running out to drink out of the water  and it gave me a real sense of  fulfillment and significance and  although it been successful in my  property business success was great but  significance was even greater since then  I've been going back and forth once or  twice a year to different African  countries finding the most needy people  that have absolutely nothing and  bringing aids and helping really poverty  in those areas because I believe that  when you are successful in business when  you have money when you're blessed your  best to be a blessing and you have an  obligation and a duty to help people  that are less fortunate than yourself so  I'm extremely excited to now say that we  have the Samuel Leeds Foundation which  is a registered charity I held off  register in this charity for so long  because I didn't want people to donate  to the charity I just wanted to pay for  it myself out of my own business profits  but people have been on my back to the  last few years saying Samuel we've seen  the work that you're doing we've seen  the lives that you change in we want to  help we want to give so that's why we've  now set up with Samuel Leeds Foundation  which is going to focus on four things  firstly is immediate aid for people that  are in need like bringing water to  people that have no clean water second  literally is education I think that when  you  grow in your knowledge and when you  learn about finance and business and  personal development what happens is  that breaks poverty is the key to  prosperity so we're teaching business  all across different parts of Africa  we're teaching budding entrepreneurs  we're teaching kids we're even working  with the government to try and partner  with them to introduce into the school  systems across Uganda at the moment  personal development and business  finance in the mainstream government  schools so that's a really really  important part of the foundation thirdly  is either the unfortunate experience of  having to have immediate emergency  surgery in Uganda in Uganda and in most  African countries there's no NHS so you  have to pay for treatment and there are  so many people that were coming into the  hospital that we're in serious needs  they were worse off than I were but they  didn't have the money to pay for their  operations and they'd just be sent home  so I've partnered again with the lady  who did the surgery on my leg I've  partnered with her and what the  foundation is doing is it's giving money  to people that are in desperate need of  operations and surgery that cannot  afford it and we're going to help work  with those people because I tell you  something nothing worse than being  absolute agony in hospital but not being  able to afford the treatment fourth  thing is most exciting potentially is  we're building schools so right now  we're building a school in Uganda  there's a lot of schools out here in the  villages whereby kids can't go to school  the schools are too far or the local  schools are just the butler building so  we're building schools out here in  Uganda and I want you to do that across  the whole nation of Africa I've no idea  how much this is gonna cost but we'll  figure that out you have an hour later  so if you want to get involved in these  projects then you can now we have this  registered foundation registered charity  it's a couple of ways you can help  firstly is you can give if you want to  give or speak to myself or the team and  we'll give you details of how you can do  that but what I'd probably encourage you  to do what's more powerful than just  giving some money is get financially  free yourself like I did and then come  out here and help out because your time  is more valuable than your money if  you're financially free as a result of  my training and you want to come out to  Africa and you want to help out again  tell me tell the team and we can bring  you out if you've got a burning desire  to come  but you haven't really got much to give  financially I believe that you can't  help the poor by being poor yourself so  get educated become financially free and  then come out from a position of  abundance actually able to give actually  able to help being able to get the time  off work because you're financially free  yourself so my mission in the UK is to  teach people to become financially free  same across Africa  that's the charity Samuel Leeds  foundation and thank you so much for  your support god bless you  [Music]
 

